var STAGE_COPY = {"1": {"title": "Form 1", "bullets": ["Protect English, Mathematics, Science and digital literacy. Every bucket uses them, even when a later programme does not formally require all four.", "Explore all 11 buckets through clubs, reading, career videos, safe practical projects and conversations with verified practitioners.", "Start a simple career notebook: interests, activities tried, skills enjoyed, subjects that need support and questions to research.", "Do not choose a single lifetime career. The Form 1 goal is exposure and foundation."]}, "2": {"title": "Form 2", "bullets": ["Complete at least one small project in three different buckets - for example a science investigation, a business budget and a creative or technical product.", "Practise communication, teamwork, punctuality, safe internet use and personal organisation.", "Ask what the student likes doing repeatedly, not only what sounds prestigious.", "Begin a portfolio folder containing certificates, projects, reflections, results and community activities."]}, "3": {"title": "Form 3", "bullets": ["Check the actual subjects offered by the school; students cannot select from the whole CXC catalogue if the school does not teach them.", "Keep English A and Mathematics whenever possible. Then protect the prerequisite subjects needed for the student's strongest two or three career clusters.", "Compare at least three future routes: a degree route, a technical/vocational route and an alternative/bridging route.", "Where available, consider CVQ/SCCP alongside academic subjects. Current Ministry policy treats academic and competency-based pathways as parallel, not inferior.", "Obtain the current programme page before final subject selection; “science stream” or “business stream” is advice, not a substitute for a named admission rule."]}, "4": {"title": "Form 4", "bullets": ["Begin CSEC/CVQ work seriously and keep SBA/project evidence organised according to current school and CXC rules.", "Join one sustained activity connected to a likely career: lab/science club, sport, debate, coding, agriculture, cadets, business, art, music, service or TVET.", "Learn to write a one-page student CV and request supervised workplace visits or job-shadowing where permitted.", "Review progress each term. A weak prerequisite subject needs early support, not panic in Form 5."]}, "5": {"title": "Form 5", "bullets": ["Sit the appropriate CSEC/CVQ examinations and maintain the portfolio.", "Apply to suitable Form 6, UG, CPCE, technical institutes, GSA, Ministry training or apprenticeship routes according to their published calendars; some institutions accept applications while results are pending.", "Compare the formal minimum, competitive reality, location, equipment, transport, accommodation, licensing and any service obligation.", "Keep a Plan A, Plan B and bridging route. One disappointing grade should trigger a revised pathway, not abandonment of the career goal."]}, "6": {"title": "Form 6", "bullets": ["Choose CAPE subjects by checking the intended programme, not by copying a friend's combination.", "Complete Unit 1 work, Communication Studies/Caribbean Studies or the school's required programme, and build research, writing and time-management skills.", "Shortlist tertiary programmes, regulators, scholarships and regional alternatives. Record deadlines and documents.", "Complete relevant Unit 2 subjects and any programme requirements.", "Apply early, request transcripts/results, prepare references and verify every condition directly with the institution.", "For regulated careers, map the full chain: education → internship/experience → examination → registration/licence → first job."]}};
